# Force LF line endings for everything text, regardless of any given
# machine's core.autocrlf setting — a Windows checkout (or `git archive`,
# which applies the same conversion) can otherwise produce CRLF-corrupted
# shell scripts, breaking bash on Linux deploy targets (e.g. a bare
# `set -euo pipefail` failing with "pipefail: invalid option name" because
# of a stray trailing \r). Git normalizes to LF in the repo either way;
# this only controls what checkout/archive hand back out.
* text=auto eol=lf
